.TH LOD.QOS_OST_WEIGHTS 4 2026-09-29 Lustre "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
lod.qos_ost_weights, lod.qos_mdt_weights \- target QoS weights
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.BI "lctl get_param lod." FSNAME "*.qos_ost_weights"
.SY
.BI "lctl get_param lod." FSNAME "*.qos_mdt_weights"
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Perms
.br
.BR 444 " | " -r--r--r--
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Per-MDT
.TP
.B Config
.br
Present in debugfs on MDS nodes
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qos_ost_weights
shows, for each OST, what the MDS uses to allocate OST objects by free
space, and
.B qos_mdt_weights
the same for the MDTs used by striped directories.
Each target is shown as a YAML list entry with these fields:
.TP
.BR ost_idx ", " mdt_idx
The index of the target.
.TP
.B tgt_avail
The free space of the target in 256-byte units, and for MDTs the free
space in 64 KiB units times the free inodes in units of 256.
.TP
.B tgt_weight
The weight of the target in the last allocation.
For OSTs this is
.B tgt_avail
adjusted by
.BR lod.qos_prio_free (4)
and limited to one stripe per file, and for MDTs it is
.B tgt_avail
less the penalties.
It is scaled down by a power of two if the largest
.B tgt_avail
is too large to sum.
.TP
.BR tgt_penalty ", " tgt_penalty_per_obj ", " tgt_last_used
The penalty of a recently used target, how much it is increased for each
new stripe, and when the target was last used, in seconds since the
epoch.
.TP
.BR svr_nid ", " svr_bavail ", " svr_iavail
The server of the target, and the free space and inodes of all of its
targets, in the units of
.BR tgt_avail :
space in 256-byte units, or 64 KiB units for MDTs, and inodes in units
of 256.
.TP
.BR svr_penalty ", " svr_penalty_per_obj ", " svr_last_used
The same penalty values for the server.
.PP
The penalty and last used values are only used for MDTs.
Writing to either file resets the weights and penalties.
.SH EXAMPLES
Show the free space and weights of the OSTs on the MDTs of the
.B testfs
filesystem:
.EX
.RB "mds# " "lctl get_param lod.testfs-*.qos_ost_weights"
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
.B qos_ost_weights
and
.B qos_mdt_weights
are part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.16.0.
.\" Added in commit v2_15_54-83-ga44956f0d57d
.SH SEE ALSO
